00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.859 align:start position:0%
we study consumers interactions when  sharing the pursuit of the same goal  customers initially joined these  programs to work on goals their values  and to seek companionship from others  who are pursuing the same goal as a  result these consumers felt close and  shared helpful tips among the group  however we found that this companionship  does not last forever once people got  near their goal and felt more certain  about their ability to pursue this goal  themselves they stopped being friends  and stopped sharing information for  example we found that Weight Watchers  members who were successfully losing  weight started sitting at the back of  the room refused to participate in  discussions stop sharing their  experiences or dropped out of the  program altogether one solution for  marketers and organizations is to  emphasize to consumers the uncertainty  in how to approach the goal to test this  solution we designed a 7 day walking  program and found that when participants  thought that they were pursuing the  walking goal for different reasons than  their partner they felt less certain  about how to approach this goal and  consequently stay friendly helpful and  share tips until the end of the program  therefore if we could make people feel  that they are still unsure about how to  lose weight the best way to quit smoking  or how to earn more frequent flyer  mileage we can foster companionship and  facilitate knowledge exchange among  consumers this way knowledge information  and tools that can help consumers attain  their goals will be shared more widely  after all we are all in the same boat
 

